## Contents

Article 21 sets out the risk management measures that essential and important entities must take. The measures shall be technical, operational and organisational and cover at least:

1. Policies on risk analysis and information system security
2. Incident handling
3. Business continuity, such as backup management and crisis management
4. Supply chain security
5. Security in acquisition, development and maintenance of systems
6. Assessment of the effectiveness of risk management measures
7. Basic cyber hygiene practices and training
8. Cryptographic measures and encryption

The article is one of the directive's most significant and forms the basis of the national requirements in member states.
